  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Initiative Against Transnational Organized Crime (GI-TOC) - Grant Migration and Displacement (2024-2029)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to strengthen community resilience against human trafficking and smuggling operations
in hotspot areas of Sahel region and Pakistan by strengthening local and regional multistakeholder networks and local civil
society responses.

To achieve the project&#x2019;s objective, the Resilience Fund will identify an agreed number of civil society actors/in-country
partners to support localised interventions. The Gi-TOC proposes two main components to empower local civil society actors
that act as first responders to human trafficking and smuggling in the absence of adequate state or international support. The
project will provide holistic support to its beneficiaries and provide platforms to share perspectives and coordinate their
programs with multi-stakeholders including at a regional level through both:

A. Direct financial support to local civil society actors (hereafter referred to as in-country partners)
B. Capacity strengthening of in-country partners</narrative>
  </description>
